# findings.jsonl — cycle_178 / adversary / 04 (TRIAGE)
# Schema: one JSON object per line, fields: {id, severity, surface, cwe, title, status, commit_pin}
# This file is intentionally a comment-only header with zero data rows.
# The card-04 spec requires a JSONL index of triaged findings; card 03 produced
# zero findings, so the index is empty. A JSON parser that skips #-prefixed
# comment lines will see an empty stream; a strict parser should treat the
# absence of data rows as "zero findings" rather than as a parse error.
